  <result aggregation-status="1" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Annual Output Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="1" ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">creation of SDG coordination mechanism</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">&#x2013; UNDP will start with elaborating a conceptual approach to designing a coordination, mainstreaming, and tracking mechanism that would be fit for purpose, be in line with the Government&#x2019;s vision and be sustainable in the longer run. This will be done in close collaboration with all relevant national level stakeholders. UNDP will begin by holding relevant consultations with the Prime Minister, Vice Prime Minister for European and Euro-Atlantic Integration and SCMU leadership. It will ensure that the newly established entity (the so-called SDG Office) integrates into the existing national strategic planning and programming machinery at the CMU level. Based on a quick analysis of SDGs mainstreaming depth, the UNDP team will identify roles for various actors, map out bottlenecks and gaps resulting in the SDG Office ToR that will contain coordination and accountability/supervision lines as well as expert profiles.

Thereafter, UNDP will work with its government counterparts to institutionalize the Office by addressing the regulatory side and hiring the experts. As the experts come on board, the wider project team will develop the SDG Office Action Plan and coordinate its rollout with the Government&apos;s key partners and kickstart the SDG Office&apos;s work. In one of its first significant deliverables, the SDG Office will conduct an SDG mapping exercise, capitalizing on the work done in preparation for the first SDG Voluntary National Review, and identify entry points for mainstreaming SDGs at different levels of policymaking and programming cycle. The SDG Office specialists will also identify and conduct consultations with relevant structures involved in policymaking and programming process on a future concept and approach for SDG mainstreaming arriving at a well-consulted concept. The process should also take into consideration the on-going efforts on improving and digitalising the system of monitoring of national reforms and strategies.</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2021">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">Until the project launch there was no SDG coordination mechanism in place at national level</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2023-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2023-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Until the project launch there was no SDG coordination mechanism in place at national level</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">SDG coordination mechanism in place at national level</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
